<title>ITALY: FORECAST-Italy money market signals o/n rate fall.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Italy money market signals o/n rate fall.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Forecasts for implicit forward rates this week show the money market expects a moderate fall in the overnight rate, a study by the Bocconi University research arm Igier showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The implicit overnight rate is seen falling in one month's time to 8.31 percent from an official market rate of 8.38 percent on Thursday, the day on which Igier based its study.</p>
<p>One week ago, the implicit overnight rate in the same timeframe was seen standing at 8.22 percent and one month ago the implicit overnight rate was forecast at 8.62 percent.</p>
<p>On a three month horizon, the implicit overnight rate is seen falling to 8.21 percent, from 8.32 percent forecast a week ago and 8.43 percent forecast one month ago.</p>
<p>The spread between the Italian implicit overnight rate and the German implicit overnight rate on a two year timeframe, considered to be a good indicator of market confidence in Europe's economic and monetary union, stands at 312 basis points from 329 basis points seen last week and 327 basis points forecast one month ago.</p>
